        "definition": "Each round reveals a predictable action set $\\mathcal A_t\\subset\\mathbb R^d$; contexts may depend on the past. The parameter $\\theta_\\star$ is fixed and unknown. $$\\|a\\|_2\\le L\\quad(a\\in\\mathcal A_t),\\qquad \\|\\theta_\\star\\|_2\\le S,\\qquad |\\langle a,\\theta_\\star\\rangle|\\le B.$$ $$Y_t=\\langle a_t,\\theta_\\star\\rangle+\\eta_t,\\qquad \\mathbb E[\\eta_t\\mid\\mathcal H_{t-1},a_t]=0.$$ Conditional on the pre-action history and current action, the noise is $\\sigma$-sub-Gaussian. The boundedness conditions needed for privacy sensitivity also require the actual action-reward pair to satisfy $$\\|(a_t,Y_t)\\|_2\\le\\widetilde L\\qquad\\text{almost surely}.$$ almost surely.",
